          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent 2-monad
            generalizes the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            by replacing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+morphism"} inverses
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoints"} adjoints
            %strong lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong KZ 2-adjunction
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monads"} 2-monads
            in the same way that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunctions"} idempotent adjunctions
            are related to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"} idempotent monads
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We will need to use all three kinds of composition in the 3-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 Cat
            %em in
            a 2-category. And we write composition along 2-cells (transformations, denoted with lower case Latin letters) with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
            %em in
            a 2-category.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⇄
                  %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \rightleftarrows D : G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjunction"} 2-adjunction
            with unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: 1_C \to G F
            and counit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon: F G \to 1_D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mi GF
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = GF
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu = G \epsilon F : M^2 \to M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi FG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = FG
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mi η
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta = F \eta G : C \to C^2
          %p
            The 2-adjunction is said to be
            %strong lax-idempotent
            if one (hence all) of the following equivalent conditions hold (of which the latter 7 are dual to the former 7; the duality involves reversing 2-cells).
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The triangle identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mo .
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_F = \epsilon F . F\eta
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\eta \dashv \epsilon F
            %li
              %p
                The induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mo .
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{G F} = G \epsilon F . G F\eta
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G F\eta \dashv G \epsilon F
              %p
                In monad notation: the induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi μ
                      %mo .
                      %mi M
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_M = \mu . M \eta
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi η
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \eta \dashv \mu
            %li
              %p
                The induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mo .
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{F G} = \epsilon F G . F \eta G
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \eta G \dashv \epsilon F G
              %p
                In comonad notation: the induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi C
                      %mo .
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_C = \epsilon C . \delta
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \dashv \epsilon C
            %li
              %p
                The induced 2-monad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = G F
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \alpha)
                has the property that the identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo .
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha . \eta_A=1_A
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ⊣
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \dashv \eta_A
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mo →
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : G F \eta \to \eta G F
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo .
                      %mi η
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w . \eta = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo .
                        %mi w
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G\epsilon F) . w = 1
              %p
                In monad notation: there is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mi M
                      %mi η
                      %mo →
                      %mi η
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : M \eta \to \eta M
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo .
                      %mi η
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w . \eta = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo .
                        %mi w
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu . w = 1
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' : G F \eta G \to \eta G F G
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' . (\eta G) = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo .
                        %mi w
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G\epsilon F G) . w' = 1
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ″
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w'' : F G F \eta \to F \eta G F
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ″
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w'' . (F \eta) = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo .
                        %mi w
                        %mo ″
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F G \epsilon F) . w'' = 1
          %p And the duals (which we will refer to below using a prime, i.e. 1’-7’):
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The triangle identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo .
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \epsilon . \eta G = 1_G
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \epsilon \dashv \eta G
            %li
              %p
                The induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo .
                      %mi F
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F G \epsilon . F \eta G = 1_{F G}
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F G \epsilon \dashv F \eta G
              %p
                In comonad notation: the induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo .
                      %mi δ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \epsilon . \delta = 1_C
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \epsilon \dashv \delta
            %li
              %p
                The induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mo .
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \epsilon F . \eta G F = 1_{G F}
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \epsilon F \dashv \eta G F
              %p
                In monad notation: the induced equality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo .
                      %mi η
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu . \eta M = 1_M
                is the counit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi η
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \dashv \eta M
            %li
              %p
                The induced 2-comonad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F G
                is colax-idempotent, meaning that every strict Eilenberg-Moore coalgebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ζ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Z, \zeta)
                has the property that the identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Z
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi Z
                      %mo .
                      %mi ζ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_Z = \epsilon_Z . \zeta
                is the unit of an adjunction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ζ
                        %mo ⊣
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta \dashv \epsilon_Z
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo :
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v : \epsilon F G \to F G \epsilon
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo .
                      %mi v
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon . v = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v . (F\eta G) = 1
              %p
                In comonad notation: there is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo :
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v : \epsilon C \to C \epsilon
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo .
                      %mi v
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon . v = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo .
                        %mi δ
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v . \delta = 1
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' : \epsilon F G F \to F G \epsilon F
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\epsilon G) . v' = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' . (F \eta G F) = 1
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ″
                      %mo :
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v'' : G \epsilon F G \to G F G \epsilon
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                      %mi v
                      %mo ″
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G \epsilon) . v'' = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ″
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mi F
                        %mi η
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v'' . (G F\eta G) = 1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_equivalence Proof of equivalence
            %p First of all, note that, by uniqueness of the left/right adjoint, most of the properties listed are (essentially) mere propositions. So we will content ourselves with proving logical equivalence.
            %p
              We first prove
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 5
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 6
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \Rightarrow 2 \Rightarrow 5 \Rightarrow 6 \Rightarrow 1'
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \Rightarrow 2
                  ) Trivial by whiskering.
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 5
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \Rightarrow 5
                  ) We have
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi η
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi μ
